  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (175 tests, 0 failed), including the new ones.\n\n- **Store (`src/store.js`):**\n  - Added `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm` and `release`. Expiry is checked only through the store's `clock`.\n  - `removeItem` now checks against available stock, so it can't remove reserved units.\n  - `confirm` also returns `{sku, stock}` so the API can reuse it.\n  - An expired reservation stays in the map. That is how `confirm` can tell `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` from `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND`. `release` removes it, and after release `confirm` reports not found.\n- **API (`src/api.js`):** `GET /stock/:sku` now includes `available`. I added the three reservation routes with the statuses you listed. `DELETE` returns `204` with a `null` body.\n- **Tests:** I added store tests and API tests for the new behavior. The store ones cover the exact expiry boundary and idempotent `release`.\n\nI didn't add validation for `ttlMs`, since the spec doesn't define it. A missing or non-numeric `ttlMs` produces a reservation that never expires, because `clock() >= NaN` is always false.",
